-- male
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[{"label":"Location","value":"Kaafu Atoll, Central Maldives"},{"label":"City Type","value":"Capital City"},{"label":"Population","value":"Approximately 140,000 residents"},{"label":"Size","value":"2.0 km long, 1.0 km wide"},{"label":"Distance from Airport","value":"10 km (via speedboat)"},{"label":"Transfer Options","value":"Speedboat, ferry, seaplane"},{"label":"Known For","value":"Capital city, cultural landmarks, government center, historical sites"},{"label":"Best For","value":"Cultural exploration, historical tours, urban experiences, shopping"}],"island_overview":["Located in the heart of Kaafu Atoll, Male City stands as the vibrant capital and cultural epicenter of the Maldives. This densely populated island city serves as the political, economic, and cultural hub of the nation, where centuries of history blend seamlessly with modern urban development to create a unique and fascinating destination unlike anywhere else in the archipelago.","What makes Male truly special is its role as the beating heart of Maldivian civilization, where traditional Islamic culture, colonial influences, and contemporary life converge in a compact urban environment. The city offers visitors an authentic glimpse into the real Maldives beyond the resort experience, showcasing the daily life, traditions, and aspirations of the Maldivian people.","Visitors to Male are drawn by its rich historical heritage, cultural landmarks, vibrant markets, diverse dining scene, architectural treasures, and the opportunity to experience authentic urban Maldivian life. The city serves as both a fascinating destination in its own right and the essential gateway to understanding the broader Maldivian culture and society."],"island_sections":[{"heading":"Location & Map","paragraphs":["Male City occupies a strategic position in the central part of Kaafu Atoll, approximately 10 kilometers from Velana International Airport. As the capital and largest city of the Maldives, Male serves as the central hub for government, commerce, education, and culture, with all major institutions and services concentrated within its compact urban area.","The city''s location provides excellent connectivity to all parts of the Maldives, serving as the primary departure point for domestic flights, ferry services, and speedboat transfers to resorts and other islands. Despite its small size, Male is one of the most densely populated cities in the world, creating a unique urban environment in the middle of the Indian Ocean."]},{"heading":"Male: Capital City & Cultural Heart","paragraphs":["Male City represents the cultural and historical soul of the Maldives, housing the nation''s most important landmarks, institutions, and cultural treasures. The city offers visitors unparalleled insights into Maldivian history, Islamic culture, and the evolution of this unique island nation."]},{"heading":"Historic Landmarks & Architecture","paragraphs":["Explore iconic landmarks including the Grand Friday Mosque, Presidential Palace, National Museum, and colonial-era buildings that showcase the architectural evolution and cultural heritage of the Maldives."]},{"heading":"Cultural & Religious Sites","paragraphs":["Visit important Islamic sites, traditional mosques, cultural centers, and religious landmarks that demonstrate the deep Islamic heritage and spiritual traditions of Maldivian society."]},{"heading":"Bustling Markets & Commerce","paragraphs":["Experience vibrant local markets, fish markets, produce vendors, and commercial districts that showcase the economic heart of the Maldives and authentic local life."]},{"heading":"Urban Maldivian Life","paragraphs":["Witness authentic urban Maldivian culture through street life, local cafes, government buildings, educational institutions, and the daily rhythms of capital city living."]},{"heading":"Major Landmarks","paragraphs":["Male''s most significant cultural and historical sites:"]},{"heading":"Cultural Experiences","paragraphs":["Authentic urban cultural activities and attractions:"]},{"heading":"Activities & Experiences","paragraphs":["Male City offers unique urban cultural experiences that showcase the authentic heart of Maldivian civilization. From historical landmarks and cultural sites to bustling markets and government buildings, the capital provides insights into the real Maldives beyond the resort experience."]},{"heading":"Historical & Cultural Tours","paragraphs":["Explore Male''s rich history through guided tours of landmarks, museums, mosques, and government buildings that tell the story of Maldivian civilization."]},{"heading":"Market & Shopping Experiences","paragraphs":["Immerse yourself in local life through visits to fish markets, produce markets, and shopping districts that showcase authentic Maldivian commerce and culture."]},{"heading":"Religious & Spiritual Sites","paragraphs":["Visit important mosques, Islamic cultural centers, and religious landmarks that demonstrate the deep spiritual heritage of Maldivian society."]},{"heading":"Urban Life & Architecture","paragraphs":["Experience authentic urban Maldivian life through street walks, architectural tours, and observations of daily life in the capital city."]},{"heading":"Day Trips & Excursions","paragraphs":["Use Male as a base for day trips to nearby islands, resorts, and cultural sites throughout Kaafu Atoll and beyond."]},{"heading":"Waterfront & Recreation","paragraphs":["Enjoy the artificial beach, waterfront promenades, and recreational areas that provide relaxation within the urban environment."]},{"heading":"People & Urban Life","paragraphs":["Male City is home to approximately 140,000 residents, making it one of the most densely populated cities in the world. This vibrant urban community represents the heart of Maldivian society, where government officials, business leaders, students, and families from across the archipelago come together to create a dynamic and diverse metropolitan environment."]},{"heading":"Capital City Dynamics","paragraphs":["As the seat of government and center of commerce, Male attracts the most educated and ambitious Maldivians, creating a sophisticated urban culture that balances traditional Islamic values with modern aspirations. The city serves as the intellectual and cultural hub of the nation, where policy decisions are made and cultural trends are established."]},{"heading":"Cultural Melting Pot","paragraphs":["Male''s population includes people from all inhabited islands of the Maldives, creating a unique cultural melting pot where different island traditions and dialects converge. This diversity, combined with international influences from diplomats, business people, and tourists, creates a cosmopolitan atmosphere unlike anywhere else in the Maldives."]},{"heading":"Urban Challenges and Innovations","paragraphs":["The city faces unique challenges related to its extreme population density and limited space, leading to innovative urban solutions and vertical development. Despite these challenges, Male maintains its cultural identity and community spirit, with strong neighborhood bonds and active civic participation in community life."]}],"island_faqs":[{"question":"What makes Male City special for cultural exploration?","answer":"Male City is the cultural and historical heart of the Maldives, housing the nation''s most important landmarks including the Grand Friday Mosque, Presidential Palace, National Museum, and UNESCO World Heritage sites. As the capital, it offers unparalleled insights into Maldivian history, Islamic culture, government, and authentic urban life. The city provides the most comprehensive cultural experience available in the Maldives, showcasing everything from ancient architecture to modern political institutions."},{"question":"What are the main attractions and landmarks in Male?","answer":"Male''s major attractions include the Grand Friday Mosque with its golden dome, the Presidential Palace, National Museum with historical artifacts, Old Friday Mosque (UNESCO site), Sultan Park, Republic Square, vibrant fish and local markets, Artificial Beach, and various government buildings. The city also offers cultural walking tours, traditional architecture exploration, and authentic market experiences that showcase the real Maldivian way of life beyond the resort experience."},{"question":"How do I get to Male City from the airport?","answer":"The speedboat is the most common and convenient option, operating regularly throughout the day. Most hotels can arrange transfers, and the journey offers beautiful views of the atoll and surrounding islands."},{"question":"What should I know about visiting Male as a tourist?","answer":"When visiting Male, dress conservatively covering shoulders and knees, respect Islamic customs especially during prayer times, and be mindful when photographing people or government buildings. The city is very walkable but traffic can be busy with motorcycles. Male offers authentic cultural experiences, excellent local cuisine, shopping opportunities, and serves as the perfect base for understanding Maldivian society and culture. Most attractions are within walking distance, and guided tours are highly recommended for historical context."}],"island_nearby_slugs":["himmafushi","huraa","dhiffushi","maafushi","gulhi","guraidhoo","hulhumale","kaashidhoo","gaafaru"]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'male';


-- manadhoo
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[{"label":"Location","value":"Noonu Atoll, Northern Maldives"},{"label":"Island Type","value":"Inhabited Local Island"},{"label":"Population","value":"Approximately 1,500 residents"},{"label":"Size","value":"1.3 km long, 0.9 km wide"},{"label":"Distance from Male","value":"190 km"},{"label":"Transfer Options","value":"Seaplane or domestic flight + speedboat"},{"label":"Known For","value":"Serene atmosphere, tranquil beaches, excellent snorkeling"},{"label":"Best For","value":"Peace seekers, nature lovers, snorkelers, cultural travelers"}],"island_overview":["Manadhoo Island is a serene local island in Noonu Atoll that offers visitors a peaceful glimpse into authentic Maldivian life. This tranquil island combines natural beauty with a calm atmosphere, providing an ideal destination for travelers seeking genuine cultural experiences and serene natural splendor.","Known for its tranquil beaches, crystal-clear lagoons, and excellent house reef, Manadhoo provides wonderful opportunities for snorkeling, swimming, and marine exploration. The island''s peaceful community embraces visitors with traditional Maldivian warmth and shares their serene way of life with genuine hospitality.","What makes Manadhoo special is its serene beauty and tranquil natural setting. Visitors can enjoy peaceful beaches, explore diverse marine life, and experience traditional island culture while staying in comfortable accommodations that showcase the serene Maldivian lifestyle."],"island_sections":[{"heading":"Location & Map","paragraphs":["Manadhoo Island is strategically located in the northern part of Noonu Atoll, approximately 190 kilometers from Male. This location provides a serene and tranquil experience while maintaining good accessibility to the capital and international airport through various transfer options.","The island''s position offers excellent protection from strong currents while providing access to peaceful coral reefs and diverse marine ecosystems. Its location in the atoll makes it an ideal base for exploring the serene beauty and cultural richness of Noonu Atoll."]},{"heading":"Manadhoo: Serene Paradise & Marine Tranquility","paragraphs":["Manadhoo Island is blessed with exceptional natural beauty, featuring pristine white sand beaches, crystal-clear turquoise waters, and one of the most serene marine environments in Noonu Atoll. The island offers perfect conditions for beach relaxation and marine exploration in a peaceful, tranquil setting."]},{"heading":"Pristine White Sand Beaches","paragraphs":["Manadhoo features tranquil white sand beaches with gentle slopes and calm waters, perfect for swimming, sunbathing, and serene beach activities."]},{"heading":"Serene House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["The island''s house reef is easily accessible from the beach and offers peaceful snorkeling with diverse marine life and colorful coral formations."]},{"heading":"Serene Community Life","paragraphs":["Experience the tranquil spirit of traditional island life with peaceful locals and serene Maldivian culture in a calm community setting."]},{"heading":"Serene Sandbank Adventures","paragraphs":["Explore nearby uninhabited sandbanks and pristine islands around Manadhoo for peaceful tropical paradise experiences with tranquil marine life."]},{"heading":"Beach Features","paragraphs":["Manadhoo''s coastal highlights include:"]},{"heading":"Marine Environment","paragraphs":["The waters around Manadhoo feature:"]},{"heading":"Activities & Experiences","paragraphs":["Manadhoo offers a perfect blend of marine adventures, cultural experiences, and serene activities. The island''s peaceful environment and tranquil atmosphere provide ideal conditions for various activities in a calm, relaxing setting."]},{"heading":"Serene House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["Explore the peaceful house reef directly from the beach, featuring colorful corals, tropical fish, and excellent underwater visibility in tranquil waters."]},{"heading":"Scuba Diving Excursions","paragraphs":["Discover nearby tranquil dive sites with professional dive operators offering guided dives and certification courses in serene marine environments."]},{"heading":"Island Hopping Adventures","paragraphs":["Visit nearby islands, pristine sandbanks, and discover the serene beauty of Noonu Atoll with peaceful exploration opportunities."]},{"heading":"Traditional Fishing","paragraphs":["Experience authentic Maldivian fishing techniques with local fishermen during sunset and night fishing trips in serene community settings."]},{"heading":"Serene Cultural Immersion","paragraphs":["Learn about local traditions, participate in community activities, and experience peaceful Maldivian island life with tranquil cultural exchanges."]},{"heading":"Sunset Cruises","paragraphs":["Enjoy magical sunset cruises around the atoll, often combined with dolphin watching and traditional dhoni sailing in peaceful waters."]},{"heading":"Community Life & Culture","paragraphs":["Manadhoo is home to approximately 1,500 residents who maintain traditional Maldivian ways of life while embracing sustainable tourism. The island''s community is known for their exceptional friendliness, hospitality, and serene cultural traditions that create a peaceful atmosphere for visitors."]},{"heading":"Island Life","paragraphs":["Daily life on Manadhoo follows traditional patterns centered around fishing, family, and community activities. The island maintains a serene atmosphere where visitors can experience authentic Maldivian culture and customs in their most peaceful, tranquil setting."]},{"heading":"Local Traditions","paragraphs":["The community preserves traditional Maldivian practices including traditional music, dance, handicrafts, and fishing techniques. Visitors can observe and often participate in cultural activities and celebrations in this serene island environment."]},{"heading":"Sustainable Tourism","paragraphs":["Manadhoo has embraced sustainable tourism practices that benefit the local community while preserving the island''s natural environment and serene cultural heritage for future generations to experience and enjoy."]}],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Manadhoo Island?","answer":"Regular ferry services are also available from Male and nearby islands in Noonu Atoll."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Manadhoo?","answer":"The best time to visit Manadhoo is during the dry season from December to April when weather conditions are most favorable for beach activities and water sports. However, the island can be visited year-round with the wet season offering fewer crowds and a more serene local atmosphere."},{"question":"What accommodation options are available on Manadhoo?","answer":"Manadhoo offers various budget-friendly accommodations including serene guesthouses and beachfront properties. Most accommodations offer air conditioning, private bathrooms, and meal packages in a peaceful setting."},{"question":"What makes Manadhoo''s community special?","answer":"Manadhoo is known for its serene and peaceful community atmosphere. The island maintains authentic Maldivian cultural practices while welcoming visitors with warm hospitality. Visitors can experience genuine cultural exchanges and participate in community activities in this tranquil setting."}],"island_nearby_slugs":["foddhoo","velidhoo","miladhoo","maafaru","landhoo","kendhikolhudhoo","magoodhoo","henbandhoo","kudafaree","lhohi","maalhendhoo"]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'manadhoo';


-- mandhoo
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[],"island_overview":[],"island_sections":[],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Mandhoo Island?","answer":"Mandhoo Island is accessible via several transportation options. The public ferry from Male operates three times a week (Sunday, Tuesday, and Thursday), departing at 9:00 AM and arriving at Mandhoo around 2:30 PM. Some guesthouses also offer private transfers for a higher fee. When planning your journey, consider that sea conditions can occasionally affect boat transfers, so it''s advisable to have some flexibility in your schedule."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Mandhoo Island?","answer":"The best time to visit Mandhoo Island is during the northeast monsoon (December-April), which generally provides the best overall weather conditions with less rainfall, lower humidity, and calmer seas. This period is ideal for snorkeling, diving, and beach activities. The water visibility is excellent during these months, making it perfect for marine life observation. The southwest monsoon (May-November) may have occasional rain showers but still offers many sunny days, fewer tourists, and lower prices. For farm tours and agricultural experiences, the period from January to March is particularly good as many crops are flourishing. Water temperature remains warm (27-30C/80-86F) year-round, making Mandhoo a viable destination throughout the year. If you''re interested in whale shark sightings in nearby areas, the period from January to April is best. For the most peaceful experience, avoid the peak holiday seasons of December-January and July-August when accommodations may be more limited."},{"question":"What makes Mandhoo different from other local islands in the Maldives?","answer":"Mandhoo stands out from other local islands in the Maldives primarily because of its strong focus on sustainability and organic farming. While many local islands offer authentic cultural experiences, Mandhoo has developed a unique identity centered around eco-friendly practices and environmental conservation. The island''s organic farms supply fresh produce to nearby luxury resorts, creating an unusual farm-to-table economy that''s rare in the Maldives. Mandhoo has implemented more comprehensive sustainability initiatives than most local islands, including renewable energy, water conservation, and waste management systems. The marine environment around Mandhoo is particularly well-preserved, with healthier coral and more abundant marine life than many more developed areas. The island offers a more tranquil experience with fewer tourists than popular local islands like Maafushi or Dhiffushi. Visitors to Mandhoo can participate in unique experiences like organic farm tours, conservation activities, and sustainable living workshops that aren''t widely available elsewhere. This combination of environmental consciousness, agricultural focus, and pristine natural beauty makes Mandhoo a distinctive destination for travelers seeking a more meaningful and responsible Maldivian experience."},{"question":"What accommodation options are available on Mandhoo Island?","answer":"Mandhoo Island offers a select range of accommodation options that emphasize sustainability and authentic experiences. Eco-guesthouses are the most common option, providing comfortable rooms built with sustainable materials and designed to minimize environmental impact. These family-run establishments typically feature natural ventilation, energy-efficient systems, and organic gardens that supply their kitchens. A few boutique lodges offer a more refined eco-experience with thoughtfully designed accommodations that blend into the natural environment. For travelers seeking an authentic cultural experience, several families offer community homestays where guests can live alongside local residents. Most accommodations offer package deals that include meals, transfers, and activities. It''s important to note that options are limited due to the island''s small size and commitment to sustainable tourism, so booking well in advance is recommended, especially during high season (December-April)."},{"question":"What marine life can I expect to see while snorkeling or diving around Mandhoo?","answer":"The waters around Mandhoo offer exceptional marine biodiversity, making it a paradise for underwater enthusiasts. The island''s house reef is particularly healthy due to local conservation efforts and limited boat traffic, featuring impressive coverage of both hard and soft coral species. Snorkelers and divers can regularly observe abundant reef fish including parrotfish, angelfish, butterflyfish, triggerfish, and fusiliers. Blacktip reef sharks are commonly seen, especially in the early morning and late afternoon, often swimming in the shallows near the beach. The area has a resident population of hawksbill and green sea turtles that can frequently be spotted feeding on coral reefs. Various ray species including eagle rays and stingrays are often seen gliding over sandy areas. Moray eels, octopuses, and various crustaceans inhabit the reef crevices, rewarding patient observers. Mandhoo''s proximity to the South Ari Marine Protected Area means that excursions to see whale sharks are possible, particularly from January to April. The waters around Mandhoo have experienced minimal coral bleaching compared to more heavily trafficked areas, resulting in healthier and more colorful reef systems. The combination of a well-preserved house reef and access to renowned dive sites in Alifu Dhaalu Atoll makes Mandhoo an excellent base for underwater exploration."}],"island_nearby_slugs":[]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'mandhoo';


