-- mathiveri
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[],"island_overview":[],"island_sections":[],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Mathiveri Island from Male?","answer":"You can reach Mathiveri Island from Male by public ferry or speedboat. The public ferry operates three times a week (Sunday, Tuesday, and Thursday), departing from Male at 9:00 AM and arriving at Mathiveri around 1:30 PM. Some guesthouses also offer private transfers for a higher fee."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Mathiveri Island?","answer":"The best time to visit Mathiveri Island is during the dry season from November to April when the weather is sunny with minimal rainfall and calm seas. The peak tourist season is from December to March, offering optimal conditions for beach activities and water sports. The wet season (May to October) sees occasional rain showers and slightly rougher seas, but still has many sunny days and lower prices. For the best balance of good weather and fewer crowds, consider visiting in November or April."},{"question":"What water sports are available on Mathiveri Island?","answer":"Mathiveri Island offers a wide range of water sports activities including snorkeling, scuba diving, kayaking, stand-up paddleboarding, jet skiing, and windsurfing. The island''s clear waters and vibrant house reef make it perfect for snorkeling right from the shore. Diving trips to nearby sites can be arranged through local guesthouses in partnership with dive centers. Equipment rental is available for most activities, and lessons can be arranged for beginners. Many guesthouses offer water sports packages that include multiple activities at a discounted rate."},{"question":"Are there any dress code requirements on Mathiveri Island?","answer":"Yes, as Mathiveri is a local inhabited island with a Muslim population, visitors are expected to dress modestly in public areas. Both men and women should cover shoulders and knees when walking around the village, visiting shops, or dining in local restaurants. Swimwear (including bikinis) is only permitted at the designated \"bikini beach\" area. When visiting the mosque or religious sites, women should cover their heads with a scarf. These dress code requirements are a sign of respect for local culture and traditions."},{"question":"Is alcohol available on Mathiveri Island?","answer":"No, alcohol is not available on Mathiveri Island. As a local inhabited island in the Maldives, Mathiveri follows Islamic law which prohibits alcohol. This restriction applies to all local islands in the Maldives. However, if you wish to enjoy alcoholic beverages during your stay, some guesthouses organize day trips to nearby resort islands or uninhabited picnic islands where alcohol is served. Alternatively, you can visit the \"floating bar\" boats that anchor near some local islands, though these are not always available near Mathiveri."}],"island_nearby_slugs":[]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'mathiveri';


-- meedhoo-dhaalu
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[],"island_overview":[],"island_sections":[],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Meedhoo Island?","answer":"Public ferry service operates weekly from Male (approximately 10-12 hours journey time). Private speedboat transfers can be arranged through guesthouses (approximately 4-5 hours from Male). Most accommodations can assist with arranging transportation."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Meedhoo Island?","answer":"The best time to visit Meedhoo Island is during the northeast monsoon season (December to April), which brings dry, sunny weather with lower humidity and calmer seas. This period is ideal for water activities, with excellent visibility for snorkeling and diving. The southwest monsoon (May to November) brings occasional rain showers but also lower prices and fewer tourists. Water temperature remains warm (27-30C/80-86F) throughout the year."},{"question":"What makes Meedhoo different from other local islands in the Maldives?","answer":"Meedhoo stands out for its rich historical heritage and traditional craftsmanship, particularly in boat building and woodworking. The island has preserved several historical sites including ancient mosques with coral stone carvings. Unlike more developed islands, Meedhoo maintains its authentic character with a community still primarily engaged in traditional fishing and crafts. The island offers access to Dhaalu Atoll''s spectacular marine life while providing a genuine cultural experience away from mass tourism."},{"question":"Are there any dress code requirements on Meedhoo Island?","answer":"As Meedhoo is a local inhabited island with a Muslim population, visitors are expected to dress modestly in public areas (shoulders and knees covered). Swimwear is only permitted at the designated \"bikini beach.\" When visiting the mosque or religious sites, women should cover their heads. These requirements don''t apply during water activities or at resort day visits. Respecting local dress codes is an important way to show cultural sensitivity during your stay."},{"question":"What historical sites can I visit on Meedhoo Island?","answer":"Meedhoo features several historical sites that offer insights into Maldivian heritage. The island''s ancient mosque showcases traditional coral stone architecture with intricate carvings. There are also historical burial sites, traditional houses that demonstrate classic Maldivian architectural styles, and community gathering spaces that have served as focal points for island life for generations. Local guides can provide historical context and stories that bring these sites to life, explaining their significance in Maldivian cultural history."}],"island_nearby_slugs":[]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'meedhoo-dhaalu';


-- meedhoo-seenu
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[{"label":"Location","value":"Seenu Atoll (Addu Atoll), Southern Maldives"},{"label":"Island Type","value":"Inhabited Local Island"},{"label":"Population","value":"Approximately 1,200 residents"},{"label":"Size","value":"1.2 km long, 0.6 km wide"},{"label":"Distance from Male","value":"540 km"},{"label":"Transfer Options","value":"Domestic flight to Gan Airport"},{"label":"Known For","value":"Authentic culture, British-era heritage, beautiful beaches"},{"label":"Best For","value":"Cultural travelers, history enthusiasts, nature lovers"}],"island_overview":["Located in the southernmost atoll of the Maldives, Hulhudhoo Island offers visitors a unique blend of traditional Maldivian culture and stunning natural beauty. As part of the Addu Atoll (Seenu Atoll) region, Hulhudhoo boasts a distinct character shaped by its southern location.","The island is known for its lush vegetation, beautiful beaches, and friendly community. Unlike many northern islands, Hulhudhoo features unique characteristics including British-era infrastructure and a more temperate climate.","What makes Hulhudhoo special is its authentic atmosphere, where visitors can experience genuine island life while enjoying comfortable accommodations and excellent snorkeling opportunities."],"island_sections":[{"heading":"Location & Map","paragraphs":["Hulhudhoo Island is part of the Addu City in Seenu Atoll, the southernmost atoll of the Maldives. This unique location gives the island distinct characteristics including a more temperate climate and British colonial influences.","The island is connected by causeways to neighboring islands, making it part of the largest connected island chain in the Maldives. This allows for easy exploration of the entire Addu Atoll region."]},{"heading":"Hulhudhoo: Natural Beauty & Marine Life","paragraphs":["Hulhudhoo Island is blessed with beautiful beaches, clear waters, and a unique marine environment shaped by its southern location in the Maldives."]},{"heading":"Beautiful Beaches","paragraphs":["Hulhudhoo boasts long stretches of white sand beaches with calm, clear waters perfect for swimming and relaxation."]},{"heading":"Marine Exploration","paragraphs":["The island''s house reef offers excellent snorkeling with diverse marine life and coral formations unique to southern atolls."]},{"heading":"Authentic Island Life","paragraphs":["Experience genuine Maldivian hospitality and traditions with a distinct southern character."]},{"heading":"Unique Ecosystems","paragraphs":["Explore the distinctive marine ecosystems of the southern atolls with guided excursions."]},{"heading":"Beach Highlights","paragraphs":["Hulhudhoo''s coastal features include:"]},{"heading":"Marine Environment","paragraphs":["The island''s underwater world features:"]},{"heading":"Activities & Experiences","paragraphs":["Hulhudhoo offers a variety of activities that showcase its unique southern atoll character and natural beauty."]},{"heading":"House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["Explore the vibrant house reef with unique southern atoll marine life."]},{"heading":"Scuba Diving","paragraphs":["Discover unique dive sites in the southern atolls with professional operators."]},{"heading":"Island Exploration","paragraphs":["Visit neighboring islands via causeways to experience different communities."]},{"heading":"Cultural Tours","paragraphs":["Learn about Hulhudhoo''s unique history and British-era heritage."]},{"heading":"Bicycle Tours","paragraphs":["Explore the connected islands by bicycle via the causeway network."]},{"heading":"Sunset Cruises","paragraphs":["Enjoy magical sunset cruises around the atoll''s unique geography."]},{"heading":"People & Community Life","paragraphs":["Hulhudhoo is home to a vibrant community of approximately 1,200 residents who maintain strong cultural traditions while embracing modern influences. The island''s population is known for their warmth and hospitality."]},{"heading":"Daily Life","paragraphs":["Life on Hulhudhoo follows traditional rhythms with fishing, craftsmanship, and family at its core. The connected nature of Addu Atoll allows for easy interaction between island communities."]},{"heading":"Culture & Traditions","paragraphs":["Hulhudhoo preserves authentic Maldivian culture with distinct southern influences. The island''s British-era heritage adds unique elements to its traditions and architecture."]},{"heading":"Local Economy","paragraphs":["The island''s economy is based on fishing, agriculture, and increasingly tourism. Many families participate in traditional occupations while also engaging in the tourism sector."]}],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Hulhudhoo Island?","answer":"Hulhudhoo is accessible via domestic flight to Gan International Airport (1.5 hours from Male), followed by a short 15-minute speedboat ride or ferry transfer to the island."},{"question":"What makes Hulhudhoo different from northern islands?","answer":"Hulhudhoo has distinct southern characteristics including British-era heritage, a more temperate climate, and unique marine ecosystems. It''s also part of a connected island chain via causeways."},{"question":"What accommodation options are available?","answer":"Hulhudhoo offers various budget-friendly accommodations including family guesthouses and beachfront properties."},{"question":"What activities are unique to this area?","answer":"Unique activities include exploring British-era heritage sites, cycling across connected islands, and experiencing southern atoll marine life through snorkeling and diving."}],"island_nearby_slugs":["feydhoo","maradhoo","hulhudhoo","hithadhoo"]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'meedhoo-seenu';


-- meedhoo
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[{"label":"Location","value":"Raa Atoll, Northern Maldives"},{"label":"Island Type","value":"Inhabited Local Island"},{"label":"Population","value":"Approximately 1,200 residents"},{"label":"Size","value":"1.2 km long, 0.7 km wide"},{"label":"Distance from Male","value":"148 km"},{"label":"Transfer Options","value":"Seaplane or domestic flight + speedboat"},{"label":"Known For","value":"Enchanting culture, stunning beaches, excellent snorkeling"},{"label":"Best For","value":"Culture enthusiasts, beach lovers, snorkelers, magic seekers"}],"island_overview":["Meedhoo Island is an enchanting local island in Raa Atoll that offers visitors a captivating glimpse into traditional Maldivian life. This mesmerizing island combines natural beauty with a magical atmosphere, providing an ideal destination for travelers seeking spellbinding cultural experiences and stunning tropical surroundings.","Known for its magnificent beaches, enchanting coral reefs, and excellent marine biodiversity, Meedhoo provides extraordinary opportunities for snorkeling, swimming, and underwater exploration. The island''s captivating community embraces visitors with traditional Maldivian warmth and shares their magical way of life with enchanting hospitality.","What makes Meedhoo special is its enchanting natural environment and captivating island setting. Visitors can enjoy stunning beaches, explore rich marine ecosystems, and experience magical island culture while staying in comfortable accommodations that showcase the enchanting Maldivian lifestyle."],"island_sections":[{"heading":"Location & Map","paragraphs":["Meedhoo Island is magically located in the northern part of Raa Atoll, approximately 148 kilometers from Male. This location provides an enchanting and captivating experience while maintaining good accessibility to the capital and international airport through various transfer options.","The island''s position offers excellent protection from strong currents while providing access to stunning coral reefs and diverse marine ecosystems. Its location in the atoll makes it an ideal base for exploring the natural beauty and cultural richness of Raa Atoll in its most enchanting form."]},{"heading":"Meedhoo: Enchanting Paradise & Marine Magic","paragraphs":["Meedhoo Island is blessed with exceptional natural beauty, featuring stunning white sand beaches, crystal-clear turquoise waters, and one of the most enchanting marine environments in Raa Atoll. The island offers perfect conditions for beach relaxation and marine exploration in a captivating, magical setting."]},{"heading":"Stunning White Sand Beaches","paragraphs":["Meedhoo features enchanting white sand beaches with gentle slopes and calm waters, perfect for swimming, sunbathing, and magical beach activities."]},{"heading":"Enchanting House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["The island''s house reef is easily accessible from the beach and offers captivating snorkeling with diverse marine life and colorful coral formations."]},{"heading":"Enchanting Island Community","paragraphs":["Experience the captivating spirit of traditional island life with friendly locals and enchanting Maldivian culture in a magical community setting."]},{"heading":"Magical Sandbank Adventures","paragraphs":["Explore nearby uninhabited sandbanks and stunning islands around Meedhoo for enchanting tropical paradise experiences with rich marine life."]},{"heading":"Beach Features","paragraphs":["Meedhoo''s coastal highlights include:"]},{"heading":"Marine Environment","paragraphs":["The waters around Meedhoo feature:"]},{"heading":"Activities & Experiences","paragraphs":["Meedhoo offers a perfect blend of marine adventures, cultural experiences, and enchanting activities. The island''s captivating environment and magical atmosphere provide ideal conditions for various activities in a stunning, mesmerizing setting."]},{"heading":"Enchanting House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["Explore the captivating house reef directly from the beach, featuring colorful corals, tropical fish, and excellent underwater visibility in magical waters."]},{"heading":"Scuba Diving Excursions","paragraphs":["Discover nearby stunning dive sites with professional dive operators offering guided dives and certification courses in enchanting marine environments."]},{"heading":"Island Hopping Adventures","paragraphs":["Visit nearby islands, stunning sandbanks, and discover the natural beauty of Raa Atoll with captivating exploration opportunities."]},{"heading":"Traditional Fishing","paragraphs":["Experience authentic Maldivian fishing techniques with local fishermen during sunset and night fishing trips in enchanting community settings."]},{"heading":"Captivating Cultural Immersion","paragraphs":["Learn about local traditions, participate in community activities, and experience enchanting Maldivian island life with magical cultural exchanges."]},{"heading":"Sunset Cruises","paragraphs":["Enjoy magical sunset cruises around the atoll, often combined with dolphin watching and traditional dhoni sailing in enchanting waters."]},{"heading":"Community Life & Culture","paragraphs":["Meedhoo is home to approximately 1,200 residents who maintain traditional Maldivian ways of life while embracing sustainable tourism. The island''s community is known for their exceptional friendliness, hospitality, and enchanting cultural traditions that create a captivating atmosphere for visitors."]},{"heading":"Island Life","paragraphs":["Daily life on Meedhoo follows traditional patterns centered around fishing, family, and community activities. The island maintains an enchanting atmosphere where visitors can experience captivating Maldivian culture and customs in their most magical, mesmerizing setting."]},{"heading":"Local Traditions","paragraphs":["The community preserves traditional Maldivian practices including traditional music, dance, handicrafts, and fishing techniques. Visitors can observe and often participate in cultural activities and celebrations in this enchanting island environment."]},{"heading":"Sustainable Tourism","paragraphs":["Meedhoo has embraced sustainable tourism practices that benefit the local community while preserving the island''s natural environment and enchanting cultural heritage for future generations to experience and enjoy."]}],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Meedhoo Island?","answer":"Regular ferry services are also available from Male and nearby islands in Raa Atoll."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Meedhoo?","answer":"The best time to visit Meedhoo is during the dry season from December to April when weather conditions are most favorable for beach activities and water sports. However, the island can be visited year-round with the wet season offering fewer crowds and a more enchanting local atmosphere."},{"question":"What accommodation options are available on Meedhoo?","answer":"Meedhoo offers various accommodations including enchanting guesthouses and beachfront properties. Most accommodations offer air conditioning, private bathrooms, and meal packages in a captivating setting."},{"question":"What makes Meedhoo''s atmosphere special?","answer":"Meedhoo is known for its enchanting and captivating community atmosphere. The island maintains traditional Maldivian cultural practices while offering a magical environment perfect for cultural exploration. Visitors can experience spellbinding cultural exchanges and participate in enchanting community activities."}],"island_nearby_slugs":["rasgetheemu","ungoofaaru","rasmaadhoo","vaadhoo","alifushi","angolhitheemu","dhuvaafaru","fainu","hulhudhuffaaru","inguraidhoo","innamaadhoo","kinolhas","maakurathu","maduvvaree"]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'meedhoo';


-- miladhoo
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[{"label":"Location","value":"Noonu Atoll, Northern Maldives"},{"label":"Island Type","value":"Inhabited Local Island"},{"label":"Population","value":"Approximately 1,300 residents"},{"label":"Size","value":"1.2 km long, 0.8 km wide"},{"label":"Distance from Male","value":"185 km"},{"label":"Transfer Options","value":"Seaplane or domestic flight + speedboat"},{"label":"Known For","value":"Vibrant community, stunning beaches, excellent snorkeling"},{"label":"Best For","value":"Cultural enthusiasts, beach lovers, snorkelers, active travelers"}],"island_overview":["Miladhoo Island is a vibrant local island in Noonu Atoll that offers visitors an energetic glimpse into authentic Maldivian life. This dynamic island combines stunning natural beauty with a lively atmosphere, providing an ideal destination for travelers seeking genuine cultural experiences and vibrant natural splendor.","Known for its stunning beaches, crystal-clear lagoons, and excellent house reef, Miladhoo provides exceptional opportunities for snorkeling, swimming, and marine exploration. The island''s energetic community embraces visitors with traditional Maldivian warmth and shares their vibrant way of life with genuine hospitality.","What makes Miladhoo special is its vibrant energy and dynamic natural setting. Visitors can enjoy stunning beaches, explore diverse marine life, and experience traditional island culture while staying in comfortable accommodations that showcase the vibrant Maldivian lifestyle."],"island_sections":[{"heading":"Location & Map","paragraphs":["Miladhoo Island is strategically located in the northern part of Noonu Atoll, approximately 185 kilometers from Male. This location provides a vibrant and dynamic experience while maintaining good accessibility to the capital and international airport through various transfer options.","The island''s position offers excellent protection from strong currents while providing access to stunning coral reefs and diverse marine ecosystems. Its location in the atoll makes it an ideal base for exploring the vibrant beauty and cultural richness of Noonu Atoll."]},{"heading":"Miladhoo: Vibrant Paradise & Marine Dynamism","paragraphs":["Miladhoo Island is blessed with exceptional natural beauty, featuring pristine white sand beaches, crystal-clear turquoise waters, and one of the most vibrant marine environments in Noonu Atoll. The island offers perfect conditions for beach relaxation and marine exploration in a dynamic, energetic setting."]},{"heading":"Pristine White Sand Beaches","paragraphs":["Miladhoo features stunning white sand beaches with gentle slopes and calm waters, perfect for swimming, sunbathing, and vibrant beach activities."]},{"heading":"Vibrant House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["The island''s house reef is easily accessible from the beach and offers dynamic snorkeling with diverse marine life and colorful coral formations."]},{"heading":"Vibrant Community Life","paragraphs":["Experience the dynamic spirit of traditional island life with energetic locals and vibrant Maldivian culture in a lively community setting."]},{"heading":"Vibrant Sandbank Adventures","paragraphs":["Explore nearby uninhabited sandbanks and pristine islands around Miladhoo for dynamic tropical paradise experiences with vibrant marine life."]},{"heading":"Beach Features","paragraphs":["Miladhoo''s coastal highlights include:"]},{"heading":"Marine Environment","paragraphs":["The waters around Miladhoo feature:"]},{"heading":"Activities & Experiences","paragraphs":["Miladhoo offers a perfect blend of marine adventures, cultural experiences, and vibrant activities. The island''s dynamic environment and energetic atmosphere provide ideal conditions for various activities in a lively, exciting setting."]},{"heading":"Vibrant House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["Explore the dynamic house reef directly from the beach, featuring colorful corals, tropical fish, and excellent underwater visibility in vibrant waters."]},{"heading":"Scuba Diving Excursions","paragraphs":["Discover nearby dynamic dive sites with professional dive operators offering guided dives and certification courses in vibrant marine environments."]},{"heading":"Island Hopping Adventures","paragraphs":["Visit nearby islands, pristine sandbanks, and discover the vibrant beauty of Noonu Atoll with dynamic exploration opportunities."]},{"heading":"Traditional Fishing","paragraphs":["Experience authentic Maldivian fishing techniques with local fishermen during sunset and night fishing trips in vibrant community settings."]},{"heading":"Vibrant Cultural Immersion","paragraphs":["Learn about local traditions, participate in community activities, and experience dynamic Maldivian island life with vibrant cultural exchanges."]},{"heading":"Sunset Cruises","paragraphs":["Enjoy magical sunset cruises around the atoll, often combined with dolphin watching and traditional dhoni sailing in dynamic waters."]},{"heading":"Community Life & Culture","paragraphs":["Miladhoo is home to approximately 1,300 residents who maintain traditional Maldivian ways of life while embracing sustainable tourism. The island''s community is known for their exceptional friendliness, hospitality, and vibrant cultural traditions that create a dynamic atmosphere for visitors."]},{"heading":"Island Life","paragraphs":["Daily life on Miladhoo follows traditional patterns centered around fishing, family, and community activities. The island maintains a vibrant atmosphere where visitors can experience authentic Maldivian culture and customs in their most dynamic, energetic setting."]},{"heading":"Local Traditions","paragraphs":["The community preserves traditional Maldivian practices including traditional music, dance, handicrafts, and fishing techniques. Visitors can observe and often participate in cultural activities and celebrations in this vibrant island environment."]},{"heading":"Sustainable Tourism","paragraphs":["Miladhoo has embraced sustainable tourism practices that benefit the local community while preserving the island''s natural environment and vibrant cultural heritage for future generations to experience and enjoy."]}],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Miladhoo Island?","answer":"Regular ferry services are also available from Male and nearby islands in Noonu Atoll."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Miladhoo?","answer":"The best time to visit Miladhoo is during the dry season from December to April when weather conditions are most favorable for beach activities and water sports. However, the island can be visited year-round with the wet season offering fewer crowds and a more vibrant local atmosphere."},{"question":"What accommodation options are available on Miladhoo?","answer":"Miladhoo offers various budget-friendly accommodations including vibrant guesthouses and beachfront properties. Most accommodations offer air conditioning, private bathrooms, and meal packages in a dynamic setting."},{"question":"What makes Miladhoo''s community special?","answer":"Miladhoo is known for its vibrant and dynamic community atmosphere. The island maintains authentic Maldivian cultural practices while welcoming visitors with warm hospitality. Visitors can experience genuine cultural exchanges and participate in community activities in this energetic setting."}],"island_nearby_slugs":["foddhoo","manadhoo","velidhoo","maafaru","landhoo","kendhikolhudhoo","magoodhoo","henbandhoo","kudafaree","lhohi","maalhendhoo"]}'::jsonb
